.An Jesús Daniel Colmenares Oviedo Aq Mt DtxdF@disroot.org
.Sh CAVEATS
Changing the backend by modifying the
.Sy SECRETS_BACKEND
parameter in your
.Xr appjail.conf 5
file does not re-encrypt data that is already encrypted. In fact, it is like
starting from scratch, since each backend uses its own data directory.
The exceptions to this are
.Sy age
and
.Sy rage Ns ,
which use the same data directory.
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
AppJail needs to decrypt data in a non-interactive manner, so it's possible that
some data, such as the keys used by the backends, may be unencrypted. If this
concerns you, you can change
.Sy SECRETS_BACKENDSDIR
to a partition or a ZFS dataset with encryption enabled.
